        "literal_source_text": "We study the problem of sampling from the probability measure \\mu(\\mathrm{d}x)=Z^{-1}e^{-V(x)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x μ ⁡ ( d ​ x ) = Z − 1 ​ e − V ⁡ ( x ) ​ d ​ x \\mu(\\mathrm{d}x)=Z^{-1}e^{-V(x)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x on \\mathbb{R}^{d} ℝ d \\mathbb{R}^{d} , where V\\in C^{2}(\\mathbb{R}^{d}) V ∈ C 2 ​ ( ℝ d ) V\\in C^{2}(\\mathbb{R}^{d}) satisfies, for 0<\\alpha\\leq\\beta 0 < α ≤ β 0<\\alpha\\leq\\beta , \\alpha I\\preceq\\nabla^{2}V(x)\\preceq\\beta I\\,,\\hskip 20.00003ptx\\in\\mathbb{R}^{d}\\,,\\hskip 20.00003pt\\kappa\\coloneqq\\tfrac{\\beta}{\\alpha}\\,. α ​ I ⪯ ∇ 2 V ​ ( x ) ⪯ β ​ I , x ∈ ℝ d , κ ≔ β α . \\alpha I\\preceq\\nabla^{2}V(x)\\preceq\\beta I\\,,\\hskip 20.00003ptx\\in\\mathbb{R}^{d}\\,,\\hskip 20.00003pt\\kappa\\coloneqq\\tfrac{\\beta}{\\alpha}\\,. (1.1) The main result of this paper is the following."
